add("ExecLedger", "executor", f"Build the draft calibration ledger at {WA}/drafts/ledger-draft.json. Read the draft claim Ca in {LANE}/reports/round-74/claims.json and the round-73 ledger {LANE}/reports/round-73/ledger.json (its schema: id, stated_at, stated_text, observe_cmd argv list, parse regex capture, expected_after, disposition REPAIR|ANNOTATE, why; plus fleet_pin and must_track). Produce >= 12 pairs at base {BASE}: RUN every observe_cmd at base now (via git -C {LANE} show/ls-tree/grep or `git -C {FLEET} show <hash>:<path>` for the fleet report) and record observed_at_base — a pair that is not red at base is dropped, never kept. Mandatory pairs: (a) '9 scenarios' (SCORECARD/LOG/fleet report) vs selftest-r3.txt '10 scenarios'; (b) SCORECARD round-73 rows asserting PASS legs for ACCEPT-C-73 / ACCEPT-CA-73 vs the absence of any PASS receipt under reports/round-73/telemetry (observable as a grep count 0 vs ledger-expected receipts); (c) the six round-73 w2 files — they are uncommitted: observe via `git -C {LANE} ls-tree -r {BASE} --name-only -- .ufo/waves/round-73/w2/` (the five modified files exist at base in OLDER form; the untracked one is absent) and compare sha256 of the base blob vs a pinned expected_after sha256 of the worktree content; (d) SHONEN.md box-1 'sources registered … 412 rows after round 56' is a historical-as-filed statement vs 804 — decide REPAIR or ANNOTATE; (e) README footers (the last footer is live). Use ONLY allowlisted observe commands (git, grep, wc, sha256sum; no python -c, no echo). Also include the sweep outputs if the ScoutLedgerSweepA/B/C reports exist when you finish ({LANE}/{W}/ScoutLedgerSweep*.md) but do not wait for them. Output JSON plus a short rationale table in your report.")
add("ExecReceiptRerun73", "executor", f"Defect routed from the round-73 closure (item 2): PASS-at-lands receipts for the round-73 counters. In a fresh clone D=$(mktemp -d) && git -C \"$D\" init -q is NOT needed for clones — instead `git clone -q {LANE} \"$D/lane\"` then run, inside \"$D/lane\" checked out detached at the round-73 lands 2d1cd9140d3a6c42296d71e4f29587582a4a88c0 (`git -C \"$D/lane\" checkout -q --detach <hash>` is allowed ONLY on this clone), `python3 -B reports/round-73/accept-c.py --root . --lands 2d1cd9140d3a6c42296d71e4f29587582a4a88c0` and `python3 -B reports/round-73/accept-ca.py --root . --lands 2d1cd9140d3a6c42296d71e4f29587582a4a88c0 --fleet-root {FLEET}` (read the docstrings and {LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-73/w2/ExecRerunC.md / ExecRerunCa.md first for the exact stamped form, including the post-report requirement). Save the full stdout/stderr, exit codes, the counter sha256, the clone's `git rev-parse HEAD` and tree hash at {LANE}/{W}/receipts/measures-c73-at-lands.txt and measures-ca73-at-lands.txt. Report whether each prints PASS at those lands and, if the Ca counter FAILs because the fleet report has since landed or been edited, say exactly which leg and why (this decides how the receipt is labelled; never alter the counter). Never run git writes in {LANE}.")
add("ExecRenumber", "executor", f"Collision guard + by-document id map, in scratch. Follow the CORPUS item-10 guard exactly: A={WA}/assimilation; grep -oE '^ {{0,3}}\\|[[:space:]]*S[0-9]{{3,}}' on {LANE}/corpus/SOURCES.md and on {STAGE}/SOURCES.append.md -> $A/reg-ids and $A/staged-ids, comm -12 -> $A/collisions (all three files written under $A). Prove the guard first: a scratch registry copy with an indented row `  | S883 | ...` (2 spaces) and a 3-space one, plus a 4-space control that must NOT collide (code block), plus a column-zero-only grep control showing it misses the indented ones — save under $A/guard-proof/ with outputs. Then state for the four theme rows whether the STAGED ids (S883, S884, S899, S900) collide with lane ids (they do: the lane holds S883/S884/S899/S900 as different documents — name each lane document) and that the adopted ids S881..S884 are absent from reg-ids as prior ids. Write {WA}/assimilation/id-renumber-map.json (old staged id -> new lane id by document with URLs) and verify the round-73 map is untouched (cmp). Also write register-id-overlap.txt (staged ids that are ALSO register ids S776..S835 and what each means). Report with exact commands and outputs. Do not touch {STAGE}.")
