add("CritCCounterVacuity", "critic", f"Attack claim C's predicate for vacuity. For each leg in {LANE}/reports/round-74/claims.json claim C, construct the cheapest do-nothing or junk landing that would pass it (two stub .md files with a header; four rows copied from staged with used-by pointing at stubs; Gate lines with quotes that are not on the page; REPOINTED satisfied by ids that name unrelated documents; evidence files carrying only a flag; a config edit in the graded tree) and say whether the leg as worded rejects it. Use the round-73 counter {LANE}/reports/round-73/accept-c.py and {LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-73/w2/MutPredicateC.md and MutLandedC.md as the reference: for each leg say what a mutant of it would survive. Give a ranked list of at most 8 predicate tightenings (exact wording) that close the survivors without making the claim unprovable.")
